  "term": "catecholamine",
  "definition": "Catecholamines are a group of hormone-like chemical messengers, including adrenaline, noradrenaline, and dopamine, that are made from tyrosine. They are produced in the adrenal glands and sympathetic nervous system, especially during stress, and help regulate many body functions.",
